# ============================================================================
# Caddyfile — TLS reverse proxy for the Smart Reception server
# ============================================================================
# The FastAPI app (server_app.py) serves the dashboard SPA, the REST API,
# and the /ws WebSocket all on a single plaintext port (default :5000).
# Caddy sits in front of it and terminates TLS, so the browser talks
# HTTPS + WSS while the app keeps speaking plain HTTP/WS on localhost.
#
# WebSocket upgrades (/ws) are proxied transparently — Caddy forwards the
# Connection/Upgrade headers automatically, so no extra config is needed.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pick ONE site block below (comment out the other), then run:
#     caddy run
# from this directory. Stop with Ctrl+C.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Option A: Local development / demo -------------------------------------
# `localhost` makes Caddy mint a locally-trusted certificate automatically
# (no browser warning on this machine). Dashboard: https://localhost
localhost {
	encode gzip
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:5000
}

# --- Option B: On-prem pilot on a LAN IP ------------------------------------
# Uncomment and set your machine's LAN IP. `tls internal` uses Caddy's own
# local CA (install it once on client devices with `caddy trust`), so other
# machines on the network reach the dashboard over HTTPS without warnings.
#
# https://192.168.1.50 {
# 	encode gzip
# 	tls internal
# 	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:5000
# }

# --- Option C: Public domain (real, auto-renewing Let's Encrypt cert) -------
# If the server is reachable from the internet on a real domain, Caddy will
# fetch and renew a trusted certificate with zero extra config.
#
# reception.example.com {
# 	encode gzip
# 	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:5000
# }
